This goal has a planning/review phase followed by a narrowly bounded coding phase. BEFORE ANY /05 IMPLEMENTATION, produce concrete canonical and frontend-snapshot type declarations for the in-scope migration and obtain explicit user approval. Findings belong in PLANROOT only; reviewing or marking the preceding audits complete does not authorize coding. The proposal must cover types needed by later slices, but approving their design does not mean implementing all of them in this goal.

User review decision: retain the existing FrontEnd registration/initialization pattern for now. Do not implement FrontendDataIndices or SessionFrontendBinding, or change initialize_frontend_state to the proposed index-only argument. That alternative is a deferred reminder, not a requirement for this phase. Any header cleanup here must preserve current initialization; do not force full removal of Session references from that existing seam by redesigning it.

After approval, implement ONLY the shared declaration/header/registration boundaries required to keep the existing ModelSelection and SessionStats examples working and to support adding approved domains later. Preserve their canonical ownership, stable addresses, existing values/display behavior, dirty_.exchange(false), independent output flags and designated numeric-change consumer. Isolate Session-specific wiring from frontend-facing declarations as approved; make minimal verified reference-contract corrections and focused tests. Keep the existing FrontEnd/Data/UnlockedData mechanism, with no new registry, generic state bag, command bus or lifecycle framework.

Not implementation scope here: adding the active-agent/directory/session domains or their writers/UI (/03), moving settings/trust/overview ownership (/04), migrating catalogs/selectors/todos (/05), relocating statistics computation or submission refresh triggers (/06), interaction compatibility work (/07), or deleting the bulk runtime snapshot (/08). Do not narrow all action callbacks or rewrite session-transition handling in this foundation phase. Preserve current history and interactive exchanges and all behavior while later slices remain unimplemented. UI-only preferences/drafts stay tui-thread-local without UnlockedData/locks.

The coding phase ends with unchanged working model/stats projections and a buildable approved shared boundary, validated by focused model/stats registration, initialization, no-op, flag-consumption and replacement tests plus applicable dependency/debug checks. Verify concurrency/lifetime only for touched paths; normal runtime simplicity takes priority over speculative shutdown remedies. Later migration goals remain independently necessary and must not be marked achieved by this groundwork. User-requested changes to approved type shapes must return to review before implementation expands.
